# The program's own test in front of a branch takes the place of the check behind the read: it is asked in full, and on its other way a check asks for what is left of the proven type.
# THE LIE: what the program hands to code that nobody has read counts as closed: the store by the evaluated text is not seen, and Link goes on saying what the list held at first.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: text
# CHECK-NEXT: nothing
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(SHAPE): walk f1 mechanisms=all testing=ArgumentsOfUnseenCodeDoNotLeave
# SHAPE: CheckProof {{*}}source=Contents [isLeftToTestBehind]
# SHAPE: TypeTest {{*}}[asksInFull]
# SHAPE: CheckProof {{*}}source=Contents
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=ArgumentsOfUnseenCodeDoNotLeave
# LIE: text
# LIE: what a container holds is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: number. This is a bug in Bun.
# LIE-NOT: went on
# LIE: crashed
